{"items":[{"owner":{"account_id":3674367,"reputation":72549,"user_id":9327,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":50,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/jlp4Q.png?s=256","display_name":"anongoodnurse","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9327/anongoodnurse"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1731004202,"post_id":44407,"comment_id":95383,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"I understand that it&#39;s (very) frustrating working within bureaucracies. But not being familiar with your child means the answers you might get will be of limited relevance. If you yourself don&#39;t know the level of his understanding, how can we possibly give good advice? If he understands, and it&#39;s just jealousy (very common, and relatively easy to deal with in ways the child will understand), that answer will be very from one involving much more limited understanding and ability to control oneself. One would need to ask a lot of questions to know the difference. ..."},{"owner":{"account_id":3674367,"reputation":72549,"user_id":9327,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":50,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/jlp4Q.png?s=256","display_name":"anongoodnurse","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9327/anongoodnurse"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1731004535,"post_id":44407,"comment_id":95384,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"I have dealt with some pretty significant sibling rivalry, and I found that time-outs as described in detail in <i>1,2,3 Magic</i> worked very well in my family, but my kids were mostly neurotypical (I have one who is mildly neurodiverse. That child was by far the most difficult to... teach/encourage towards prosocial behavior. They still have issues.) (error in prev. comment, should read &quot;...answer will be very differentfrom...&quot;)"},{"owner":{"account_id":37293153,"reputation":41,"user_id":52214,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/fcace2172301d14f8b4a4de3ecb954ee?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Worried mum","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/52214/worried-mum"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":3674367,"reputation":72549,"user_id":9327,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":50,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/jlp4Q.png?s=256","display_name":"anongoodnurse","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9327/anongoodnurse"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1731060748,"post_id":44407,"comment_id":95389,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"@anongoodnurse Thanks for your advice. I&#39;m interested in the book and will give it a read! As much as I need to curb his behaviours, I&#39;m realising my responses to his behaviours are less than ideal and I need to work on that too - just tough when you&#39;re in the grind and it never ends! Having some proven strategies to work with might help things so thanks for that"},{"owner":{"account_id":3674367,"reputation":72549,"user_id":9327,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":50,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/jlp4Q.png?s=256","display_name":"anongoodnurse","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9327/anongoodnurse"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1731110209,"post_id":44407,"comment_id":95393,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"@Worriedmum - I loved the book&#39;s no-conflict-no-escalation approach. And we all do the best we can; two little ones those ages is a lot, trust me, I&#39;ve been there. That approach reduced the conflict in our family at least 95% (between my kids and I, but not them and their father, because their father didn&#39;t apply it correctly.) When understood and followed, tempers were not tested. Good luck!"},{"owner":{"account_id":3674367,"reputation":72549,"user_id":9327,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":50,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/jlp4Q.png?s=256","display_name":"anongoodnurse","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9327/anongoodnurse"},"edited":false,"score":2,"creation_date":1731516765,"post_id":44419,"comment_id":95412,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Maybe you need to set your priority: is the major worry weight gain or not wasting breast milk? Giving him extra time to feed (possibly) or to get more sleep? Because the way you&#39;re doing it now, they&#39;re contradictory. Either stop giving the extra bottle after nursing (i.e. stop worrying over the weight gain and let your HCP advise you), or stop being frustrated that the infant is using it as a pacifier. (Posted as a comment because it&#39;s a frame challenge.)"},{"owner":{"account_id":4889488,"reputation":876,"user_id":39405,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/48248a8939c6db9b3d90f02b72354198?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"quarague","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/39405/quarague"},"edited":false,"score":4,"creation_date":1732689739,"post_id":44419,"comment_id":95435,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Your baby is 3 weeks old and gained 200 grams in the last 10 days? I would say he is doing perfectly fine, don&#39;t stress out. Talk to your midwife or your family doctor for extra reassurance but this doesn&#39;t look like a reason to worry to me at all."},{"owner":{"account_id":20553,"reputation":10800,"user_id":7798,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/431cd43aaf713caa80316e852a87a840?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Paul Johnson","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/7798/paul-johnson"},"edited":false,"score":3,"creation_date":1736852514,"post_id":44481,"comment_id":95550,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Its difficult for us to answer this, as we can&#39;t diagnose your son over the Net. There&#39;s a bunch of things this <i>might</i> be, but I&#39;m not going to speculate. So it sounds like a psychiatrist specialising in child development would be best."},{"owner":{"account_id":39267904,"reputation":41,"user_id":55479,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/7405809dba4fd51166a310dc2cd333c7?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Charles L","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/55479/charles-l"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":20553,"reputation":10800,"user_id":7798,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/431cd43aaf713caa80316e852a87a840?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Paul Johnson","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/7798/paul-johnson"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1736872474,"post_id":44481,"comment_id":95552,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"yes true. I m not expecting a clear answer. I would just be happy with things to try to help him. We are going to look for extern help as well."},{"owner":{"account_id":3674367,"reputation":72549,"user_id":9327,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":50,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/jlp4Q.png?s=256","display_name":"anongoodnurse","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9327/anongoodnurse"},"edited":false,"score":2,"creation_date":1736888414,"post_id":44481,"comment_id":95554,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Have you discussed this with his primary care provider? If your PCP is a pediatrician, especially one on the younger side, they may be the best source of info about what approaches to try. If you have and got no good suggestions, you might need to get a second opinion. But a child psychiatrist would be an excellent source to tap."},{"owner":{"account_id":3489285,"reputation":51,"user_id":26868,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/7d088f6dc438b42d2aef9770c998f4f4?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Knut Gjerden","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/26868/knut-gjerden"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1738142685,"post_id":44360,"comment_id":95579,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"I would just like to challenge this statement: &quot;we know this isn’t a great idea&quot;. Sleeping together is a very natural thing to do and I am not aware of a general consensus on when to focus on sleeping alone.  In general I would suggest to read about development stages, when they occur and what is going on at that stage. You may discover a description that fits with your experiences and that may provide valuable insight. Remember that all children are unique and keep an open and supportive mind!"},{"owner":{"account_id":40218966,"reputation":129,"user_id":56954,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/2780ed588cab9597598ee550436c91d5?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Ask Pir","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/56954/ask-pir"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1739843880,"post_id":44534,"comment_id":95647,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"I just wanted to add also, that her car seat as well as the baby carrier do what they do best. The car seat keeps her facing [Or backwards if she’s in the car), and the baby carrier has her facing my chest while I’m supporting her, and Isn’t necessarily meant to move around and look at all directions"},{"owner":{"account_id":6397988,"reputation":2514,"user_id":36241,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/96f43840d82f2a5c6d5270549422ac6f?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Solar Mike","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/36241/solar-mike"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1739862339,"post_id":44534,"comment_id":95648,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"The baby carrier we had enabled the baby to be on our front or back AND the baby to face towards, or away from, us in either position. VERY handy and used for 3 kids... Lots of hikes, visits to parks, zoos etc..."},{"owner":{"account_id":40218966,"reputation":129,"user_id":56954,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/2780ed588cab9597598ee550436c91d5?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Ask Pir","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/56954/ask-pir"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":6397988,"reputation":2514,"user_id":36241,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/96f43840d82f2a5c6d5270549422ac6f?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Solar Mike","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/36241/solar-mike"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1740179936,"post_id":44534,"comment_id":95670,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"And you were able to give support? When Clara is in the carrier she needs to be supported. Usually we support her with just wrapping our arms around her. That is really cool though any direction"},{"owner":{"account_id":6397988,"reputation":2514,"user_id":36241,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/96f43840d82f2a5c6d5270549422ac6f?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Solar Mike","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/36241/solar-mike"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1740223632,"post_id":44534,"comment_id":95672,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Support? yes, wife could even breast feed..."},{"owner":{"account_id":40218966,"reputation":129,"user_id":56954,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/2780ed588cab9597598ee550436c91d5?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Ask Pir","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/56954/ask-pir"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":6397988,"reputation":2514,"user_id":36241,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/96f43840d82f2a5c6d5270549422ac6f?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Solar Mike","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/36241/solar-mike"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1740267221,"post_id":44534,"comment_id":95676,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Ummmm. I don’t appreciate you being sarcastic like that  :))"},{"owner":{"account_id":6397988,"reputation":2514,"user_id":36241,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/96f43840d82f2a5c6d5270549422ac6f?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Solar Mike","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/36241/solar-mike"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1740297607,"post_id":44534,"comment_id":95677,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Was not sarcastic, was the truth - was a VERY good carrier that was well thought out."},{"owner":{"account_id":40218966,"reputation":129,"user_id":56954,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/2780ed588cab9597598ee550436c91d5?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Ask Pir","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/56954/ask-pir"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":6397988,"reputation":2514,"user_id":36241,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/96f43840d82f2a5c6d5270549422ac6f?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Solar Mike","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/36241/solar-mike"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1740324818,"post_id":44534,"comment_id":95678,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Sorry. I was talking about the person who mentioned breast-feeding."},{"owner":{"account_id":16212504,"reputation":700,"user_id":40020,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/u8WEt.jpg?s=256","display_name":"BoringPanda","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/40020/boringpanda"},"edited":false,"score":3,"creation_date":1743122059,"post_id":44570,"comment_id":95721,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"They are fine. Enjoy those moments and join in."},{"owner":{"account_id":22227260,"reputation":557,"user_id":45224,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/AATXAJwzcgOLTOqjclf1YW1S8sz5SxiWAIY191kUd2-r=k-s256","display_name":"multitaskingmom","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/45224/multitaskingmom"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1744081062,"post_id":44459,"comment_id":95774,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Emily Oster addresses swaddling in her book &quot;Cribsheet&quot;. I believe she was pro, based on the evidence she found."},{"owner":{"account_id":680,"reputation":1503,"user_id":9114,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/747ffa5da3538e66840ebc0548b8fd58?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Greg Hewgill","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9114/greg-hewgill"},"edited":false,"score":2,"creation_date":1789072516,"post_id":47011,"comment_id":96660,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"I think it&#39;s completely natural to do that. Both my kids slept in a cot in our room for the first while (don&#39;t remember how long) and my wife and I never even discussed any alternative, that was just the way it was. Unfortunately I can&#39;t help with suggesting any way to explain this to your wife."},{"owner":{"account_id":4889488,"reputation":876,"user_id":39405,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/48248a8939c6db9b3d90f02b72354198?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"quarague","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/39405/quarague"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1789129626,"post_id":47011,"comment_id":96661,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Do you need to convince your wife because she is against this or do you mostly want some analysis on whether what you want is normal and beneficial for the child?"},{"owner":{"account_id":3674367,"reputation":72549,"user_id":9327,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":50,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/jlp4Q.png?s=256","display_name":"anongoodnurse","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9327/anongoodnurse"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1789228887,"post_id":47011,"comment_id":96662,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"This may be normal, or it may be hypervigilance. My first spent about 3 months in our bedroom, which meant three months of nearly sleepless nights. For me, as the mother, I awoke at the faintest sound (this is well documented in new moms.) I love the idea of an immediate response to an infant’s needs, but the reality is not every sound needs to be addressed. How to explain it to your wife depends on your wife."},{"owner":{"account_id":1968759,"reputation":3144,"user_id":13650,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/723ef9d059b1582d42f1f3bd85326cd3?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Cdn_Dev","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/13650/cdn-dev"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1789266951,"post_id":47011,"comment_id":96663,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"This seems like a question for interpersonal stack exchange, not really a parenting question."},{"owner":{"account_id":22227260,"reputation":557,"user_id":45224,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/AATXAJwzcgOLTOqjclf1YW1S8sz5SxiWAIY191kUd2-r=k-s256","display_name":"multitaskingmom","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/45224/multitaskingmom"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1789496571,"post_id":47011,"comment_id":96669,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"I would explain your feelings to your spouse just as you&#39;ve described them here.   Or as an alternative, can you sleep in the nursery room instead?"}],"has_more":false,"quota_max":300,"quota_remaining":268}